            <ArticleTitle>Primary psoas muscle abscess in pregnancy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>607-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1479-828X.2008.00921.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary iliacus-psoas muscle abscess formation is very uncommon during pregnancy. We present a case of a primary iliacus-psoas muscle abscess in pregnancy causing back pain with delayed diagnosis and treatment. Understanding the clinical presentation of iliacus-psoas muscle abscess helps with considering it in the differential diagnosis of back pain during pregnancy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
